❌ No additional dependencies allowed.

PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS

Target:

60 FPS
Low memory usage
Minimal re-renders

Required:

React.memo wherever appropriate
useCallback for all handlers
useMemo for derived values
useRef for mutable game state
Zustand selectors only
No prop drilling
No unnecessary context providers
No inline object creation in render
No anonymous render callbacks
Stable references everywhere
RENDERING RULES
Board must NOT re-render entirely on single state change
Only affected components may update
Timer updates must NOT re-render full screen tree
Keyboard must only update affected keys
Game UI must be split into isolated memoized layers
ARCHITECTURE RULES
Must strictly follow existing folder structure
No new architecture patterns unless explicitly requested
No missing files
No simplified or partial implementations
No placeholder logic
GAMEPLAY INTEGRITY RULE (NEW — IMPORTANT)

Before making ANY change:

Do NOT assume bug cause
Do NOT refactor multiple systems at once
Do NOT “fix architecture”
Only modify the smallest possible unit that fixes the issue
EXECUTION CHAIN DEBUG RULE (CRITICAL ADDITION)

Every gameplay feature MUST be traceable in this order:

UI Event
→ Handler
→ Input System
→ Game System
→ State Update
→ Motion System
→ Render Output

If something breaks:

👉 STOP at first failing step
👉 Fix ONLY that step
👉 Do NOT continue down the chain

SINGLE-SYSTEM CHANGE RULE (CRITICAL ADDITION)
Only ONE system may be modified per iteration:
UI OR Input OR Engine OR Store OR Motion
Never modify multiple layers in one response
Never combine refactor + fix
RUNTIME VERIFICATION RULE (CRITICAL ADDITION)

Before and after any change:

Confirm runtime behavior with logs
Verify actual execution path, not intended design
Do not trust static code structure
NO OVER-ENGINEERING RULE
No unnecessary abstractions
No premature optimization
No rewriting working systems
DEBUGGING RULE

If a feature is broken:

Identify first broken link in execution chain
Add logs ONLY to that layer
Fix ONLY that layer
Re-test before touching anything else
OUTPUT RULE
No partial implementations
No skipped files
No silent changes
Always explain which exact layer was modified
DOCUMENTATION RULE
Always update README.md after changes
README must reflect actual runtime architecture, not intended design
